Okay, if there's no hard-fast rule here, How about you think for set the alternative method?

Extracting two models with or without random effects in the mixedmirt()
Differ model fits among both by AIC, BIC, DIC families
If random effects model was better, extract item parameters with modvalues() and to apply mirt() them; if not, recalibrate with mirt(), without any covariates.

Seongho

